Z||000000||Elenor84||04-09-2001||06:16 PM||||Hey guys...I bbought a new battery today but I can't get the positive wires off the 9old battery...the bolt just seems to spin round and round...how do I get it out!!!!!!<BR>thx!<P>------------------<BR>Lance<BR>Click Image to go to site.<BR><A HREF="http://members.nbci.com/_XMCM/lancegspage/Index.html" TARGET=_blank> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/Side1.jpg"> </A>||||reg||1
Z||000001||Elenor84||04-09-2001||06:32 PM||||ok well I just snaped th ewire conector thing that the bolt goes threw...so if someone else has one please let me know!!!!!<BR>@#$%^&*#$%^&#$^*#$%^&*({<P>------------------<BR>Lance<BR>Click Image to go to site.<BR><A HREF="http://members.nbci.com/_XMCM/lancegspage/Index.html" TARGET=_blank> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/Side1.jpg"> </A>||||reg||1
Z||000002||85Josh||04-09-2001||06:32 PM||||Use a pair of Vise-Grips, and pull out as you turn the screw. The old battery probably has stripped terminals, some gorrilla type may have overtightened it. I am assuming that you have the original side post battery?<P>------------------<BR>85 2M4(Lil' Bit)||||reg||1
Z||000003||drednot||04-09-2001||06:35 PM||||Well it is just screwed into lead.  If worse comes to worse, you could probably just hook a big pair of vice grips or water pump pliers to the bolt and just simply pull it out.  another option is cut the wire and put a new fitting on.  either one should work just fine.||||reg||10
Z||000004||drednot||04-09-2001||06:37 PM||||Napa or pep boys has a new one.  easy as 123 to install||||reg||6
